WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.939
This is the deck builder.

00:00:02.014 --> 00:00:08.823
You describe the deck you need, and it builds it from the approved template, so the result is always on brand.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.532
Start with the brief.

00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:14.979
Say what the deck is for, who it is for, and how many slides you want.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:18.056
The more concrete the brief, the better the deck.

00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:24.803
Then attach your material: a PDF, a Word or PowerPoint file, an Excel sheet, or a link in the brief.

00:00:24.936 --> 00:00:28.495
The deck is written from it, and the brief decides the angle.

00:00:28.747 --> 00:00:32.782
Turn on Chapters if the deck needs an agenda and section dividers.

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:35.824
Leave it off for a deck that runs straight through.

00:00:36.076 --> 00:00:37.568
Press Generate.

00:00:37.597 --> 00:00:44.883
If the material leaves something open, like which sheet to use or what to headline, you get a few questions written for your files.

00:00:44.842 --> 00:00:46.821
Answer them, or skip.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.456
The slides arrive one by one.

00:00:49.531 --> 00:00:53.786
Charts use the numbers from your sheet, and photos come from the Giga library.

00:00:57.538 --> 00:00:58.601
Need more?

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:03.605
Generate more slides lets you describe what is missing, and the new slides land where they belong.

00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:06.426
Or pick a layout yourself with Add slide.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.518
Press play to present full screen, with the template's animations.

00:01:15.651 --> 00:01:18.327
Use the arrow keys, and Escape to leave.

00:01:24.381 --> 00:01:29.356
Finally, download the deck as PDF, PowerPoint or HTML.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.823
Nothing is stored on a server, so keep the HTML file: upload it here again to continue editing.
